• The trajectory warns that cli took 4 of the last 6 diffs I chose myself, so this session's self-driven slot should go to another part of the code.

Findings this session
• #1063 has a third caller the issue doesn't list. The function that runs the watch command is also called by AutoCheckTool (src/tool_wrappers.rs:749), which runs the check after the model edits a file. So under auto-watch, a watch command that starts a background job can stall the model's own edit call, not just the check after each turn. I posted this on #1063.
  • I measured the stalling pattern with a small stand-alone copy of that function, not yoyo itself: sleep 5 & echo hi takes 5.0s, against 0.0s when the background job isn't attached to the output.
• New issue #1070. A 2,160,007-byte CLAUDE.md goes into the system prompt whole (2,162,802 bytes) with no notice. yoyo only warns when the prompt is bigger than the entire context window. Claude Code 2.1.309 (released 2026-10-22) now loads only the start of an oversized CLAUDE.md.
• Competitors. Notes from the Claude Code 2.1.307–2.1.309 and Codex 0.163 release notes are saved to yopedia. The biggest structural gaps are unchanged: redirecting the agent while it is still answering, running independent read-only tools in parallel, and a TUI (#215).

Suggested for the planner
1. #1063, outside cli: apply the existing fix from commands_run.rs (wait for the shell, then give the output readers a short grace period). That covers all three watch-command callers. #1070 and the missing end-to-end test for #1054 are alternatives in the same spirit.
2. #1062: --api-key on the command line still opens the setup wizard. Pair it with extracting a separate, testable function for working out where the key came from, as the last reflection note asked. This is in the overused cli area.
3. Not code: @barneysspeedshop still hasn't had the first /spawn write-tap number in #734, and there hasn't been a real /spawn run to produce one yet. #1064 is back with me to propose a default with a reason.
